# 서장 + 1장 (4판) 영어판: 퀘스트 ID -> (제목, 받을 때, 진행 중, 끝낼 때). build.py 가 story.json 의 한국어 원문과 짝지어 넣는다.
EN = {
"story_0_01": ("The Dock After the Storm",
 "You came in on the ship that beat the storm, right? Welcome, Storm Survey Corps! I'm Morris, the guide. The Ember Order called you from across the sea because we're short of hands. First let me show you how to live in Emberhaven. Follow the 'Path of the Novice Adventurer' to the end.",
 "Finish every step of Morris's 'Path of the Novice Adventurer'.",
 "Well done! You're one of Emberhaven's people now. The bank, the shops, the land are all yours. Funny thing, though. Every Corps ship meets a storm on the way in. And not one comes in with a torn sail. The sailors say the storm circles the ship once and just leaves. As if it were having a look. Oh, and the Order was looking for the new surveyors."),
"story_0_02": ("A Surveyor's Trade",
 "So you're off this ship. Captain Roran. …The cane? A twenty-year-old leg. Never mind it. The Corps doesn't run on swords alone: a smith forges, a cook boils the soup, a fisher reads the sea. Go see Albert the job guide and choose your road.",
 "Talk to Albert the job guide and come back.",
 "Good. Those who pull their weight stay. I can't travel far any more. My work is making sure you eat and have a place to come back to. The Elder is waiting for the new faces."),
"story_0_02b": ("Embers and Names",
 "Welcome. I am Erwin, Elder of the Ember Order. (He offers a gloved hand.) Before the oath there is something to learn: what we guard, and why we fight only inside a Memory Gate. I have opened a practice gate in the yard. Hear me out, then look at it yourself.",
 "Listen to Elder Erwin's lesson, then examine the practice Memory Gate beside you.",
 "You saw it. The scarecrow inside is not real. It is the scarecrow the Flame remembers. Guardians are put to rest the same way, only inside a gate. Break the body outside and the seal bursts. …One day you will see a sea that paid that price. Now, the oath."),
"story_0_03": ("The Apprentice's Oath",
 "To work for the Order you must take the apprentice's oath. Fetch the oath scroll from Isabel the archivist. She was born and raised in the archive; I taught her letters myself. Then recite it before me: \"Guard the fire, guard the seals.\"",
 "Get the oath scroll from Isabel the archivist.",
 "\"Guard the fire, guard the seals.\" …Good. Take this ember. It will hold on to your name once. Stop by the kitchen before the soup goes cold. Not for me, I can't take hot food. Sleep early tonight. On the first night everyone has… the same dream."),
"story_1_01": ("The Torn Chronicle",
 "Surveyor, there's something I'd like you to look at. This is the Order's Ashen Chronicle, the story of how seven kings divided the world's fire a thousand years ago. Pages are missing here and there. People say they fell out with age… please look for yourself. And the mural on the archive wall, too. The 'price' the Elder spoke of is painted there.",
 "In the archive, examine the cut pages of the Chronicle and the mural.",
 "Knife marks, aren't they? Someone cut them out. Fifteen years ago my mother Elena, the archivist then, went looking for these pages and never came back. Her last note is one line: 'The first page, beside the broken gate.' …I have never been outside the archive. Will you come with me?"),
"story_1_02": ("The First Page Outside",
 "The 'broken gate' is a ruined hellgate, the black stone frames studded with gold that stand in the fields. Your compass will point the way. I'm coming too. …Captain Roran tied my bootlaces. He checked them three times.",
 "Find a ruined hellgate and examine what is left on it together with Isabel. (The survey compass points the way.)",
 "\"Seven caged the fire, and the fire caged one.\" It's the first page. An ink dot in the corner… the same as in the book at the archive. It was the mark Mother left wherever she found something. She stood here. Right here."),
"story_1_03": ("An Ink Dot in the Dirt",
 "There was Mother's writing on the back of the page: 'Ruins on the old road, a mark on a pot.' Trail ruins. If you brush the dirt away you find pottery sherds. I've only read about brushing. Please find me one sherd.",
 "Brush a pottery sherd out of the trail ruins and bring it back. (A brush is made of a feather, copper and a stick.)",
 "This is the one. A date beside the ink dot: spring, fifteen years ago. And a name, 'Dowin, miner'. …But wasn't that ruin strange? The village's name isn't anywhere in the Chronicle. Just like the village on the mural."),
"story_1_04": ("The One Who Stays Last",
 "Dowin the miner? I know that name. It's still on the tavern's tab. He went into the old mine fifteen years ago and never came out. Where those tunnels lead… I don't know. But miners carve words into the timbers. Go and read them. There are spiders, bring milk.",
 "Find the abandoned mine and examine the words carved into the timber.",
 "'I sent Elena on to the desert. I stay here.' …So Dowin was the guide. He sent her ahead and stayed behind alone. A guide isn't the one who goes first. He's the one who stays last. (Roran shifts his grip on the cane.) Have the archivist write that name down."),
"story_1_05": ("The Archivist's First Meal Outside",
 "I wrote Dowin's name into the Chronicle. And then… I got hungry. Strange. In the archive it was always cold bread, but after walking outside I want something warm. Grilled fish and bread will do. Eat with me.",
 "Bring 2 cooked cod and 2 bread. (From the restaurant, or by fishing and cooking.)",
 "(Isabel counts the bones as she eats.) It's good. The Elder never eats with us. He says he can't take hot food. It's been that way since I was little. …Mother liked fish. That isn't written in the Chronicle. That's something I know."),
"story_1_06": ("I Don't Know",
 "The archivist is going to the desert? Then I'd better drill you first. Take on the withered things in the fields. The desert? Never been. I only know the southern woods, the snowfields and the sun lands. Saying 'I don't know' when you don't is a captain's job.",
 "Defeat 6 zombies in the fields at night.",
 "Not bad. You saw it, they follow the living. The Elder says it's because they want their names called. I don't know. I only know people who know. …Count heads twice. Once going out, once coming back. That much I do know."),
"story_1_07": ("The Chest Opened First",
 "Dowin sent Mother to the desert. The second page should be under a desert pyramid. The books say the floor pattern hides a trap. I'm coming. I packed two water flasks this time.",
 "Find a desert pyramid and examine the traces left in the chamber below.",
 "\"The king of the desert took the eye in the sand, the king of frost the eye in the ice.\" The second page. But someone was here first. Someone besides us is following Mother's marks. And not long ago."),
"story_1_08": ("The Song on the Banner",
 "Crossbow bolts and heavy boots. The Ashen Band. In town they just call them pillagers. Their watchtowers overlook every village. Why would they count scraps of paper? Because someone pays. Hit a tower and see what they were paid.",
 "At a pillager outpost defeat 6 pillagers and examine the tower's banner.",
 "Grey coins. Money I've never seen. And that song… not a song bandits sing. Show the coin at the town hall, they have a nose for money. Take the song to the archivist. I don't understand either."),
"story_1_09": ("The Grey Coin",
 "Surveyor, may I see that coin. The town hall keeps a specimen of every currency that has ever passed through Emberhaven.",
 "Show the grey coin to Haru the town clerk.",
 "Let me sum up. One, this coin is in no record. Two, the same bounty was posted twice, in two different hands. Three, the front and the back were struck from different dies. There may be more than one person paying. Ledgers cannot lie."),
"story_1_10": ("The Mapmaker Under the Igloo",
 "Mother had one more companion: Felix the mapmaker. In the margin of the first page it says 'Felix left at the infirmary in the snow.' The cellar under an igloo. Left there… so he was ill. They say a zombie villager is locked in down there. A potion of weakness and a golden apple can bring one back. Gold is the metal that doesn't forget a name.",
 "Find an igloo, cure the zombie villager in its cellar, and examine the infirmary's records.",
 "It was Felix. Fifteen years in that cellar… thank goodness. Truly. But the signature in the record, the drawing of a hand. A gloved hand, you say? …All the old physicians must have signed that way. They must have."),
"story_1_11": ("The Man Who Can't Eat Meat",
 "Felix can't eat anything. The smell of meat alone turns him white. He won't say why. …I think he's wondering what he ate for fifteen years. Please bring something warm with no meat in it. Beetroot soup and baked potatoes.",
 "Bring 1 beetroot soup and 3 baked potatoes.",
 "(Felix stares into the soup for a long time, then takes a spoonful.) He ate. The whole bowl. Then he asked for paper. He wants to draw a map. He says the hand remembers the road it walked, even when the head forgets."),
"story_1_12": ("The Torn Map",
 "Felix stopped drawing. He got as far as the swamp and after that it's all in pieces. He needs more paper and ink. And… please stay with him. His hands shake each time a memory comes back.",
 "Bring 6 paper and 2 ink sacs, and watch Felix piece the map together.",
 "The swamp witch. Mother got 'invisible ink' from her. Now I know why some journal pages are blank. And Felix remembered one more thing. There were four of them. Mother, Dowin, Felix… he can't recall the fourth one's face."),
"story_1_13": ("The Witch's Ink",
 "The witch of the swamp hut makes invisible ink. She takes glow ink sacs as payment. Only… she doesn't tell customers from thieves very well. I leave how you get it to you. But do examine the ink jar.",
 "Find a swamp hut, examine the ink jar, and bring 3 glow ink sacs.",
 "'Shows only under blaze light.' Mother wrote her journal that way on purpose, so no one could read it in secret. But what is the purple ink at the bottom of the jar? 'Belongs to the people in the mirror'… there are no such people in the Chronicle."),
"story_1_14": ("The Burning Sky",
 "Beacon light. You'll need blaze rods, then. They are in Hell: the sunken kingdom of Caldera, the place people call Hell. Roran told you to dress for snow? Ha, he has never been. It is hot. Very. It is your first crossing, so I will go with you. Open the gate, step through, and look at the sky.",
 "Open a hellgate, enter Hell and examine its sky, then bring 3 blaze rods.",
 "(The Elder said nothing all the way back.) …Give the rods to Isabel. The lamp in the archive was the one Elena kept lit. I need to rest. Whenever I see that sky I… no, I am startled like a man seeing it for the first time."),
"story_1_15": ("The Lamp That Never Went Out",
 "We have the rods and the ink. Mother's room is at the very back of the archive. I haven't gone in once since she vanished. The lamp is still dark. …Will you come with me? I can't make myself take the doorknob alone.",
 "Light her mother's lamp together with Isabel the archivist.",
 "'Three ends from which no one returns.' The burning fortress, the city where sound dies, the end of the void. She hid them where whoever hunts the pages couldn't follow. Mother walked all three. So will I. I'm done with only reading."),
"story_1_16": ("Three Orders",
 "The first end is the fortress in Hell. Felix knows the way. The journal says: 'The fortress is not a castle but a dike. Read the three order slabs and you will know what the Black Star is.' I can't go this time, the Elder forbade it. Tell me everything you read.",
 "Find a hell fortress and examine the three order slabs.",
 "Charge, hold, get the people out first. Three captains gave three different orders. Hargen, Isolde, Merwin. Their names aren't in the Chronicle. It says the Flame Knights had four captains, but the names are scorched away. …Four. Who was the fourth?"),
"story_1_17": ("Withering and the Antidote",
 "Trouble. Felix came back from the fortress cut by a black skeleton. The wound is withering black. No ordinary poison. Poison I'd know. The ones who knew this sickness must have left something in the fortress barracks, since they're the ones who caught it. Read the barracks wall and brew an antidote. Fast.",
 "Examine the barracks scrawl in the fortress, defeat 5 wither skeletons, and bring 1 antidote for Felix. (Brewed from a glass bottle, charcoal, sweet berries and a brown mushroom.)",
 "(As Felix swallows the antidote the black fades from the wound.) He'll live. So the charcoal draws out the ash. The ash of a burnt name. …Then those black skeletons were people. Knights who never left their posts. I know men like that."),
"story_1_20": ("Standing on Those They Meant to Save",
 "Mother copied something in the fortress into her journal. The Oath of Three Heads. 'When the wall is breached, set the three captains' heads upon soul sand.' The three captains become one sentinel of their own will. Soul sand is… the ash of Caldera's people whose names the fire ate. The sentinel rises on top of the people it was meant to protect. Mother hid the page 'beside the Black Star's heart'. It can only be taken by waking it. And the journal has one more line: 'Waking them is the only way to free them.'",
 "Bring 3 wither skeleton skulls and 4 soul sand.",
 "Three heads… Hargen, Isolde, Merwin. The knights who walked their posts for a thousand years were carrying their captains' heads between them. Let's open a Memory Gate. It isn't bound to a seal, but the Black Star erases the name of everything it touches. We can't wake it near the town."),
"story_1_21": ("The Black Star",
 "The Black Star. The mural says 'when the Black Star rises the fire goes out.' Not only the fire. To it, everything alive looks like fire. It can't tell friend from foe. The three heads move apart because the three captains are still arguing. Knock the skulls back. Keep moving. Beyond the Memory Gate only you and your party fight.",
 "Open the Memory Gate and put the Black Star (the Wither) to rest.",
 "As the star cooled a scorched page fell. Elena's page. And one star left behind. They say it's three names set hard. Take it to the archivist. It isn't over until she writes them."),
"story_1_22": ("Three Names",
 "Show me the star. …It's warm. What falls asleep inside a gate is let go by the Flame. With nothing holding it, the world slowly begins to forget its name. So I write it. The fire can't eat a written name. Stay and watch.",
 "Watch Isabel the archivist write down the three captains' names.",
 "It's done. Hargen, Isolde, Merwin. And one empty line. The fourth captain's place. …If you dream tonight, tell me what the burning knight says. Somehow I think he'll say something different."),
"story_1_23": ("What Was It Called",
 "Surveyor! Everyone's celebrating. You beat that, that thing… what was it called? I knew yesterday. The black… black what? Strange. Anyway! The restaurant owner is treating everyone. And listen about the eastern fields. The patrols saw something odd.",
 "Hear the town's news from Morris the guide.",
 "Something to laugh off, right? It isn't just me. At the restaurant they all just say 'that black thing'. Only the archivist says it clearly. …Oh, the fields. The Ashen Band is gathering. More than a few."),
"story_1_24": ("When the Bell Rings",
 "The Ashen Band is coming. This one is mine. Bad leg or not, I can command. Bram the smith picked up his hammer. Go with him and break their vanguard in the eastern fields. Don't ring the town bell. They come to the sound. The archivist knows why.",
 "Together with Bram, defeat 1 ravager and 4 vindicators.",
 "Head count. Two out, two back. Good. The one we caught said Captain Kas's men keep what they gather in catacombs underground. Nobody searches among the dead. And he said something odd: 'We didn't come to steal. We came to collect.'"),
"story_1_25": ("The Note on the Coffin",
 "The catacombs. Find out what they came to 'collect'. It's crawling with zombies. Hiding things among the withered is clever. Nobody wants to stay long.",
 "Find the catacombs underground, defeat 8 zombies, and examine what lies on the coffin.",
 "Tonight, the archive? …Go back right now! I'll count heads, run!"),
"story_1_26": ("The Burning Archive",
 "Surveyor! The archive… it's on fire! I can't see through the smoke. Mother's records are still on the shelves… and there, Mia the apprentice has collapsed! We can't save both!",
 "Enter the burning archive and go to Isabel the archivist.",
 "…The fire is out. You chose what to save first. Both were right. The names written in the burnt books… only I know them now. If I forget, they're gone. And Kas took the back pages of the journal."),
"story_1_27": ("Where the Fire Began",
 "Everyone says the Ashen Band set the fire. But it's strange. Why would people who came for the pages burn the place the pages are in? I'm an archivist. I write only what was seen. Look at where the fire began with me.",
 "In the burnt archive examine where the fire started, the footprints on the floor and the scorched wall.",
 "It wasn't arson. It was an accident. And Kas stopped running, went back, and carried one of his men out, when we could have arrived any moment. …I'll write it. As it was seen. Whoever that record favours."),
"story_1_28": ("Fortress of the Dead",
 "Kas went into the undead fortress underground. Like a true evoker he lives among the withered. Open the way before the journal pages reach the grey cloak. Skeleton archers in every hall. If you see the grey cloak… don't chase. Not yet.",
 "Find the undead fortress underground and defeat 8 skeletons.",
 "No grey cloak. Kas is alone in the innermost room. He sent his men away, the wounded first. …Not what a bandit chief does. In the open he pours out vexes. Let's pull him alone into a Memory Gate."),
"story_1_29": ("Captain Kas",
 "Captain Kas. Open the Memory Gate and pull only him in. He is no guardian. He won't turn to ash if he falls inside. He'll drop outside the gate still breathing. Watch the fangs rising from the floor. The totem he holds is a sliver of ember handed down for generations. He'll get up once.",
 "Open the Memory Gate and defeat Captain Kas (the evoker).",
 "His pack. The journal's back pages. And this is a map. Old. Twenty years at least. …Wait. This signature. Roran, Kael. My name. This is my expedition's map. (Roran is silent a long while.) …He's tied up. Decide with the archivist what to do with him. She's the one who was wronged."),
"story_1_30": ("The One Who Came to Collect",
 "I talked with Kas. Even tied up he sang that song from the banner. 'We had a king.' To him the Chronicle wasn't money. It was his people's family record. The fire… he said he was sorry. He made no excuses. Surveyor, I'm angry. But I don't know that he was wrong. Decide with me.",
 "Decide together with Isabel the archivist what to do with Captain Kas.",
 "It's decided. Either way I'll write his name. Kas, captain of the Ashen Band. A man who tried to repay what was taken by taking. And a man who went back into the fire and carried his own out. I'll write both. That's what a record must do."),
"story_1_31": ("The Code of Silence",
 "The journal's back page: 'Deep dark below, the city where sound dies. I buried the page before the door.' An ancient city. They say it was the city of Velas, the King of Silence. Why a whole city forbade sound, the Chronicle doesn't say in a single line. Go and read it there. Walk crouched. One sound and something wakes.",
 "Find an ancient city and examine the Code of Silence and the roll of residents. (Walk crouched.)",
 "A city where no name could be spoken aloud. People were called by numbers. The king buried the names the fire ate, and sculk grew over them. It reacts to sound… because it is waiting for its name to be called. It wasn't frightening. It was sad."),
"story_1_32": ("Echoes Don't Forget",
 "Mother left her voice in the city's echo shards. 'An echo does not forget what it heard.' Please gather the shards. I want to… hear her voice. For fifteen years I've only read her handwriting.",
 "Bring 3 echo shards.",
 "(The shards knock together and give a faint voice.) …That's Mother. Lower than I thought. I remembered a higher voice. My memory was wrong. The shard is right."),
"story_1_33": ("Mother's Voice",
 "Trouble. The archivist is gone. I counted twice. Gone. She took the echo shards down into the ancient city alone, to hear more of her mother's voice. I can't take those stairs. This leg makes noise. You go. Crouch past the sensors and bring her back. Do not run.",
 "Crouch past a sculk sensor in the ancient city and bring the archivist back. (Advancement 'Sneak 100')",
 "(Isabel grips the shards with shaking hands. Roran silently counts. Two.) …I'm sorry. From inside the door Mother's voice called my name. But Mother never called me 'Isabel'. Always 'Bel'. That wasn't Mother."),
"story_1_34": ("That Which Calls Names",
 "The thing before the door is the gatekeeper the King of Silence set there. It was in the Code: it lets no one live who speaks a name. It mimics the voices it swallowed. Elena's is in there too. Open the Memory Gate. It has no eyes. It finds you by sound.",
 "Open the Memory Gate and put the gatekeeper warden to rest.",
 "As it fell, the voices it had swallowed scattered all at once. Hundreds of people said their own name once and were gone. A page came out of the dirt before the door. \"The eighth seat is empty. It was the seven who emptied it.\" …An eighth. The Chronicle has only seven."),
"story_1_35": ("The Day of Silence",
 "A surveyor, are you. Oscar, fisherman. The archivist girl is sitting out on the dock. Third day without a word. She only talks by writing. I know how to sit by someone who won't speak. You cast a line. Catch a few cod and sit a while.",
 "Catch 3 raw cod and bring them to Oscar.",
 "She held out a slip of paper. 'I feel someone will die if I make a sound.' So I told her the sea swallows every sound, it's safe here. …She laughed. Out loud. I light a lamp on the ice every night myself. Who am I waiting for? I'll tell you when the northern sea thaws."),
"story_1_36": ("The Empty Shelf",
 "The last end is the void. (The Elder hands over a fistful of ender eyes. On his glove they all look one way.) Throw these and they fly to the stronghold underground: a prison and a library built around the door to the void. Elena passed that door too. She did not pass the door back. When you see the library… no. See for yourself.",
 "Find the stronghold with the ender eyes and examine the library shelves.",
 "So you saw the empty shelf. …What books stood there? I don't know either. (He straightens his glove.) Truly. That one thing even I do not know. When you find the page bring it to me first. It will be too heavy for Isabel."),
"story_1_37": ("Elena's Fourteen Days",
 "The void. Mother camped in a tower city on the outer islands, away from the dragon. She wrote a line on the wall each day. Fourteen days. Please read them in order. I… I'm coming this time. I haven't told the Elder.",
 "Find an end city and examine Elena's camp records in order.",
 "Mother knew the dragon was waiting for someone. And she was preparing the rite to wake it when… the record stops on the fourteenth day. The tower's scribes hide in boxes, believing that what is shut away isn't forgotten. …Who on earth were the people of this city?"),
"story_1_38": ("The One Missing",
 "Mother made three crystals and was one short. We'll make the fourth. An end crystal: glass, an ender eye, and a ghast tear. The weeping of Caldera's people goes into it. It's a rite to welcome someone home… so I think tears are right. Show me just one. Keep four more for the pedestal.",
 "Craft one end crystal and show it to Isabel the archivist. (Keep four more for the corners of the pedestal.)",
 "Just as Mother drew it. The dragon of the void isn't out fighting from the start. It sleeps on the pedestal, hard as stone. Place crystals on the four sides and it wakes. …Don't tell the Elder yet. I will read the last page first."),
"story_1_39": ("The Rite of Return",
 "Waking the dragon. The archivist says it's no gatekeeper but a bound beast. Bound things are savage. They bite even the hand that frees them. Place the crystals on the four sides of the exit pedestal. The crystals on the towers heal it, break them first. The whole void is the battlefield, so the whole expedition goes. Only those who deal 10% of its health are counted. Heads… I'll count when you're back.",
 "Place the crystals to wake the dragon of the void, and put it to rest. (Deal at least 10% of its health.)",
 "It cried out as it fell? Long, once. Not like its fighting roar. …The echo shard took the sound down. It's still trembling. A leather cover came out of the dirt under the pedestal. Elena's last page. I didn't open it. The archivist reads it first."),
"story_1_40": ("Mother's Last Line",
 "You brought the last page? …The Elder asked to see it first. No. I must read this first. Read it with me. This time I want to read to the end. After I write the dragon's name. I don't know its name, so I'll write what was seen.",
 "Read the last page of the journal with Isabel the archivist.",
 "On the fourteenth night, while the dragon slept, Mother buried the page and never made it back to the tower. …What became of the last line was your choice. Thank you. Either way. I'm not only a reader any more."),
"story_1_41": ("The Ember Oath",
 "So you walked all three ends. The first since Elena. I recognise the Corps as full apprentices of the Order. Recite the oath before me again. The third line too, this time. …And where is Elena's last page?",
 "Recite the oath to Elder Erwin.",
 "\"Guard the fire, guard the seals. And…\" You can't recall the third line? Ha, never mind. That line was never there. Isabel will keep the last page? …Yes, that is right. (The gloved hand trembles for a moment.) Go and see the captain now. That map will weigh heavily on Roran."),
"story_1_42": ("What Is Reflected",
 "Surveyor, look at this. I brought Mother's things back from the camp in the void. There was a cracked crystal orb among them. Mia the apprentice screamed while polishing it. She saw a person in it, she said. Someone swinging a sword. Mia has never held a sword. Look into it with me.",
 "Look into the crystal orb together with Isabel the archivist.",
 "There was a note of Mother's in the cloth around it. 'Handed to me by the people in the boxes of the scribes' tower. I don't know what it is. Hold a light to it and forgotten handiwork shows.' A mirror that reflects the skills of forgotten people, it seems. Who made it and why, I don't know. Set on a stand, anyone can look into it. Take one. Handle it gently. It's cracked."),
}
